<!--MachineBlocks — SCAD documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.TypesAndSerialization-->
<scad:TypesAndSerialization xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml"
  xmlns:mbt="com.machineblocks.bml.type"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A guide to MBOM type serialization for SCAD
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Status: Draft — MBOM type shapes are defined in com.machineblocks.bml.type.*; SCAD serialization
    rules continue to be validated against the V3 library. Prefer BML type definitions over
    Markdown/YAML for shapes; this block summarizes the serialization strategy only.
    
    Strategy: take the canonical MBOM value → validate → normalize → emit the shortest valid SCAD
    form → wrap as ["paramName", value] in settings/config.
    
    Typical SCAD forms (details live on the type Blocks):
    AxisXYZ — scalar, [xy, z], or [x, y, z]
    AxisXY — scalar or [x, y]
    Per-side-4 — scalar, [x, y], or four-value array
    FaceVector6 — always six values
    FaceMap — [["face", value], …] (optional namespaced keys)
    SelectiveGrid — [base, [[rect], value], …] or a scalar broadcast
    
    Do not design MBOM around SCAD arrays. Design SCAD arrays as serialization of MBOM.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="scad:ScadDecisionRules" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — SCAD decision rules and mb_block() capability boundary.
    </see>
    <see type="mbml:TypeSystem" relation="SeeAlso">
      Domain type package overview.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:SizeXYZ" relation="Defines">
      Example type — see BML definition for shape.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:AxisXYZ" relation="Defines">
      AxisXYZ container type.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:SelectiveGrid" relation="Defines">
      SelectiveGrid container type.
    </see>
    <see file="domains/machineblocks/machineblocks-v3-scad-target/runtimes/scad-lib/docs/05_types_and_mapping.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Historical mapping notes — follow BML types when they diverge.
    </see>
  </references>
</scad:TypesAndSerialization>
